 {
  "id": 11070,
  "iid": 768,
  "project_id": 17,
  "title": "Local Kernel Stacks",
  "description": "#196 \n\nAs it currently is, the kernel stacks can be allocated from any NUMA domain without taking into account the domain in which the CPU is located. This can result in constant remote accesses (ignoring hardware optimisations) throughout the lifetime of the kernel (which for workstations and servers might be many days or weeks) since the stack pages are some of the most frequently accessed ones.\n\nThis MR causes the kernel stack pages to be allocated from the same node as the CPU on which the kernel runs.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-11-06T12:33:20.169Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-11-10T12:31:34.322Z",
